<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Formalization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="Analysis of Attention Patterns. ‣ 4 Results and Discussions ‣ What do vision-language models see in the context? Investigating multimodal in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we analyze the attention patterns in different VLMs. Here, we formalize how we aggregate the attention scores in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.1 </span>Attention per Token Type</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, given <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{(h,d)}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{(h,d)}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> the attention score from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th token at <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-th attention head for the <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample, a sequence of textual and visual tokens <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(t_{1},v_{1},\ldots,t_{k},v_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(t_{1},v_{1},\ldots,t_{k},v_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and a sequence of response tokens <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the attention score per token type <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{a}_{i,j}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}|}\frac{1}{H}\sum_{d}\sum_{h}a^{(h,d)}_{i,j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>d</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>h</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{a}_{i,j}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{D}|}\frac{1}{H}\sum_{d}\sum_{h}a^{(h,d)}_{i,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{T_{k}}=\frac{1}{|R|}\sum_{i\in R,j\in T_{k}}\bar{a}_{i,j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{T_{k}}=\frac{1}{|R|}\sum_{i\in R,j\in T_{k}}\bar{a}_{i,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of response tokens, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{D}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{D}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> represent the dataset size and the number of heads, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.2 </span>Attention per Visual Token</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the average attention matrix across all heads and samples, denoted as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{a}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.2.1 Attention per Token Type ‣ A.2 Formalization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ What do vision-language models see in the context? Investigating multimodal in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we define the average attention per visual token as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{V}=\frac{1}{|V|}\sum_{0\leq i&lt;N,j\in V}\bar{a}_{i,j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{V}=\frac{1}{|V|}\sum_{0\leq i&lt;N,j\in V}\bar{a}_{i,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of visual tokens and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens in the sequence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.2.3 </span>Attention Entropy</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the average attention matrix across all heads and samples, denoted as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{a}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.2.1 Attention per Token Type ‣ A.2 Formalization ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ What do vision-language models see in the context? Investigating multimodal in-context learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we define the attention entropy as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}=-\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sum^{N}_{i=1}\sum^{N}_{j=1}\bar{a}_{i,j}log(\bar{a}_{i,j}+\epsilon)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>l</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=-\frac{1}{N^{2}}\sum^{N}_{i=1}\sum^{N}_{j=1}\bar{a}_{i,j}log(\bar{a}_{i,j}+\epsilon),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens in the sequence, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
